WEBVTT

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.190
The fourth match in the Autumn Selection,

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:09.570
between Candidate Takumi Aldini and Candidate Mimasaka Subaru,

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.030
will be a Cooking Battle!

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.250
A Cooking Battle in the middle
 of the Autumn Selection?!

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.710
Is that even allowed?

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.710
There is no question that
 the conditions have been met.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:28.050
The administration has deemed this an official Cooking Battle!

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:28.590
I see.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.890
A Cooking Battle is not restricted by time or place. Such is its nature!

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.850
So far, five judges have made a joint decision on the outcome in this tournament.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.940
However, an exception was made for this match, so each judge will cast one vote.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.650
The match will thus follow 
the Cooking Battle format.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:45.930
A Cooking Battle.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:48.360
The candidates will now enter the arena!

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.170
Wow.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.450
Bro...

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:59.210
It must be hard, having an 
incompetent younger brother.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:01.980
Pick it up.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.610
What?

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:06.380
I'll teach you proper manners, since you lack any.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.810
If you pick that up, it means you have accepted the challenge.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:14.430
This is how we conduct duels—the duello.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:18.530
Italians always seek 
vengeance after humiliation.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.270
If I win, I'll have you grovel 
and apologize right here,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.560
to the mezzaluna you've tainted,

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.020
and to my brother!

00:01:28.990 --> 00:02:59.080
{OP}

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:53.610
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:01:53.610 --> 00:02:00.080
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.830
An endless journey

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:08.840
Let's hone each other's pride

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.340
Words aren't really important

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.840
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:20.810
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:23.180
No reason

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.690
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:28.440
We're reckless challengers

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:33.440
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.990
A swordsman should use his blade

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:38.820
To open the way to the future

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:44.540
This is my story and no one else's

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.040
Hey!

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.150
Yukihira!

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.310
Megumi!

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.960
Where've you been? Jeez!

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.680
W-Well, we were with Takumi-kun and
 Mimasaka-kun until just a short while ago,

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.220
but they didn't say anything about a Cooking Battle.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:20.630
Mimasaka intended to make this into a Cooking Battle from the very start.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.390
That's the kind of guy he is.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.890
He does exhaustive research on his targets,

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:31.570
then uses any means necessary,
 be it provocation or intimidation,

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:33.730
to drag them into a face-off.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:38.160
He has already won ninety-nine Cooking Battles in that manner.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:39.870
Ninety-nine...

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.410
The theme is dessert!

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.500
Let the cooking begin!

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:51.670
Their ingredients...

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.670
They're exactly the same!

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:58.380
I have brought the records on Mimasaka Subaru's previous Cooking Battles.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.010
It lists the dishes made by both sides.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.810
What?!

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:08.690
He's always won by serving the exact same dish as his opponent!

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.050
Semifreddo.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.990
That's what you and I are going to make.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:21.860
Semifreddo is as cold 
in temperature as ice cream,

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.370
and as soft in texture as cake.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:29.270
This semifreddo will have 
a topping of scattered pralines,

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:32.620
an "ice cream" layer 
with meringue and heavy cream,

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.380
and a sponge cake layer. 
A triple-layer type.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.590
Did I get that right?

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:39.690
Hmph.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.840
So that's what you got out of stalking me.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:45.060
You think you can win if you have the same recipe?

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:49.230
<i>Never underestimate an Aldini!</i>

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:54.940
Mimasaka plays around with the Cooking Battle system as his toy.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:59.910
He makes his opponents wager a chef's most important possessions: their tools.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:04.330
By robbing them of their tools,
 he obliterates their pride.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.450
Does he think of himself 
as Musashibou Benkei?{a Japanese warrior monk (sōhei) who served Minamoto no Yoshitsune and collected 999 swords from opponents - unless you want a ridiculously long TL note, put this in the release blurb}

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:08.950
What a stinker.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:15.000
One story has it that he took a cherished knife
 that had belonged to his opponent's late mother,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.840
while laughing maniacally.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:23.270
That means Takumi-kun put 
his mezzaluna on the line.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.920
Th-There's nothing to worry about!

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.140
Just look at him.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.150
He's not showing any hesitation!

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.980
Yeah! His movements are meticulous!

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:37.190
If you screw up measurements in any way when making sweets, the taste is ruined.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:40.000
That's why you need a lot of attention to detail.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.150
A hulk like Mimasaka wouldn't—

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:43.820
What?!

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.790
H-He's very meticulous.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:50.790
It's almost as though he's...

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.870
...a girl doing embroidery!

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:58.090
Hasta la vista, Aldini.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.670
This is where I'll start adding twists!

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:06.930
Takumi-kun's beating the egg yolks and egg whites together,

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:11.430
but Mimasaka-kun's beating them separately when making the batter.

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.440
<i>Mimasaka Subaru conducts an exhaustive investigation of his opponents.</i>

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.900
<i>He gathers any and all information about recipes they are testing</i>

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.070
<i>to predict what his opponent
 will attempt to make.</i>

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:27.530
<i>He then adjusts his version of the dish to raise himself one step above his opponent.</i>

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:33.530
A "pâte à génoise" cake, made by beating the yolk and whites together, has a moist, delicate crumb.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.480
In comparison, a "pâte à biscuit" cake,
 made by beating them separately,

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:38.560
has a very airy crumb,

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:41.550
so it will absorb a lot of syrup,
 resulting in great texture.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:46.890
My version will be able to maximize the benefits of this divine syrup.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:50.820
You chose a smooth, gentle texture.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:53.730
Because that's what you 
always did back in Italy.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:59.690
But when these two are compared, mine will have a stronger flavor.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:03.290
So by adding such 
twists in selected areas,

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:07.160
he decreases his probability of losing 
until it's close to zero.

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:10.620
So you're making the syrup next, right?

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.330
With this {liquor}liqueur?

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.960
<i>He even has the limoncello!</i>

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:18.750
It's Italian {liquor}liqueur made from lemons.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:24.080
Rum and amaretto 
are typically used in the syrup,

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.340
but he's using the same 
ingredient, even here.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.930
He knows about the limoncello panna cotta.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:33.640
Your family restaurant, Trattoria Aldini,

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:36.810
has a specialty dish that makes heavy use of this.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:42.060
That's why I figured you'd 
use this in the semifreddo.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.150
<i>Does he really see right through me?</i>

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.350
I've added other twists too.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:54.870
My custard will have mascarpone in addition to heavy cream, for added richness.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:59.380
It's the same thing you did with the curry pasta you made in the prelims.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:04.590
How does it feel to be outpaced by someone
 using your own special skill?

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:06.350
Director!

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:08.570
Should such a match even be allowed?

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:11.550
In a Cooking Battle, the food is everything.

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:15.390
There is no reason to remonstrate
 Mimasaka Subaru for his behavior.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:19.470
<i>Mimasaka Subaru only cares about winning.</i>

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:22.230
<i>That is why he goes 
"right down to the last detail."</i>

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:25.940
<i>He profiles his opponents 
in order to become them.</i>

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:30.160
Emotional guys like you 
make the easiest opponents.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.620
You may look cool and calm on the outside,

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.500
but you are passionate about your cooking.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:40.210
You have much affection 
and pride for your homeland,

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:42.630
and that will always show in your dishes.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:47.840
I'm glad you're exactly 
as I made you out to be.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:52.050
<i>He continues to observe his opponent, and exposes who they are.</i>

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:57.390
<i>Mimasaka Subaru is the King of Stalkers!</i>

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:01.270
He's even more dangerous than I thought!

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:04.770
Takumi has to come up with a new twist too!

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.240
But does he even have time for that?

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:08.780
Is he just gonna lose?

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:11.530
Bro is flexible. He got that 
from working in the kitchen.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.530
An Italian wouldn't lose a dolce match!

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:18.950
<i>My intended recipe is totally known to him.</i>

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.160
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.390
<i>Make something completely new from scratch?</i>

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:24.530
<i>No, I don't have time for that.</i>

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:25.900
<i>Is there something I can do?</i>

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:26.920
<i>Is there nothing I can do?</i>

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.530
<i>Once I put the batter in the oven,</i>

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:32.470
<i>I can't add any twists to it.</i>

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:36.250
<i>Should I add chopped lemons 
to improve the fragrance?</i>

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:39.350
<i>No, that would ruin the important texture.</i>

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.700
Hey, don't you have to start baking soon

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:44.580
if you want to finish in time?

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:50.850
Takumi put his batter in the oven too!

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:54.280
Now he can only make alterations to the toppings and the sauce.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:10:00.290
But Takumicchi doesn't have any 
ingredients he can use to add a twist!

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.840
<i>I have limited time.</i>

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.290
<i>I have to proceed with the dish.</i>

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.670
<i>I'm being constrained by the very tracks I laid down!</i>

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:11.590
We now have less than thirty minutes left.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.880
Both of them are done with baking!

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:15.770
Huh?

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:19.550
Is Mimasaka's cake darker than Aldini's?

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:20.720
You're right!

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.020
Why?

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:24.230
Biscuit joconde.

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:29.530
Most of the flour has been replaced by almond flour.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:32.990
It results in a more fragrant, rich sponge.

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:34.990
<i>Another twist!</i>

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:38.320
<i>Hah. The greater their pride,</i>

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:41.180
<i>the greater their paralysis
 when they realize they're in a crisis.</i>

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:44.410
<i>They're afraid to serve a dish they know will lose.</i>

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:48.710
<i>You're the same way, aren't you, Aldini?</i>

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:51.320
<i>If I lose now...</i>

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.200
<i>Why did I even come here to Japan?</i>

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.020
<i>Bro!</i>

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:09.140
<i>Don't look like that, Little Brother.</i>

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.540
<i>Remember the Aldini kitchen.</i>

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:14.820
<i>The din and clamor...</i>

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:17.860
<i>Have faith in what you learned there!</i>

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.430
<i>Let's show them.</i>

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:27.660
<i>With this match, I'll surpass
 the person I've been until now...</i>

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.700
<i>and the recipes I've made until now!</i>

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.090
All right, it's done.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.050
So beautiful!

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:43.510
Is this the semifreddo that will 
surpass Takumi Aldini's dish?

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:44.430
Hm...

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:47.970
The praline is fragrant with almonds.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:52.060
The ice cream-like layer is half-thawed frozen cream.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.560
All very delicate work.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:55.400
Hmph!

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:58.190
Cobbling together various surface inspirations!

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.740
I doubt the flavors will 
form a cohesive whole.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:02.570
Well, let's give it a taste.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.450
<i>The difference in textures 
created by the three layers...</i>

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:09.580
<i>I can tell just by inserting 
a spoon into the dish!</i>

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:14.580
<i>The fresh sweetness 
of the lemons fills my mouth,</i>

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.170
<i>and the fragrant almonds 
entertain my sense of smell!</i>

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:20.840
<i>The flavors have been melded together without any off flavors—impressive!</i>

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:27.300
<i>How sweet and mellow! 
My inner girlishness is coming out.</i>

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:32.810
I went with biscuit joconde because it pairs perfectly with praline.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.980
You can detect the fragrance and
 richness of almonds in the sponge—

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.150
Quiet!

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:39.020
Do you have no principles as a chef?

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:41.990
I struggle to understand what you mean.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:46.910
"Down to the last detail." That is my credo.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.950
I did not spare any effort in analyzing my
 opponent's capabilities and planning my victory.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.540
What do you find wrong about that?

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.460
<i>I don't want to acknowledge him.</i>

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.960
<i>I don't want to!</i>

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.800
<i>But I can't resist the allure.</i>

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.010
<i>What a despicable guy...</i>

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.340
<i>Despicable... Despicable...</i>

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:10.720
<i>Despicable... Despicable... Despicable... Despicable... Despicable...!</i>

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.270
<i>I hate him! He's so cool!</i>

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.980
<i>But his smile makes my heart spin.</i>

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.230
<i>Still, I have to ask.</i>

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:20.860
<i>Please step on the love accelerator 
with your desserts.</i>

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:24.700
<i>Despicable... Despicable... Despicable...</i>

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.530
<i>I turned into a girl 
without even thinking about it!</i>

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:34.000
<i>It's the ultimate dessert that feels like an amplification of Aldini's hotness.</i>

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.460
<i>How can he hope to win now?</i>

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:39.670
Oh?

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:41.880
What, you're going to serve them your dish?

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.630
Don't underestimate me.

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.380
I'm a professional.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.800
No matter what happens,
 we serve food to our customers.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.220
That dish...

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:53.720
It's different from the semifreddo I saw Bro testing.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:55.060
You're right.

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:58.520
There's a very thin layer between the cream and sponge layers!

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.270
A fourth layer!

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:14.580
<i>Please...</i>

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.250
<i>come!</i>

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:21.170
<i>How vivid!</i>

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.130
<i>It's a Mediterranean breeze!</i>

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:29.970
I've eaten many semifreddos,

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.600
but this is different from all of them!

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.970
Where is this overwhelming
 lemon flavor coming from?

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:37.680
What is this golden layer?!

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:42.270
That is lemon curd,
 a condiment with roots in England.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:43.820
Lemon curd.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:46.570
Some types are procured 
for use by the British royal family.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:48.240
It has a very long history.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:52.200
This elegant paste is fragrant with the sweet-sour flavor of lemons.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:57.040
It melts in your mouth 
with the fine génoise sponge.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:00.120
What a light mouthfeel!

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:02.750
The grainy biscuit joconde
 could never be this soft!

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:09.680
Lemon curd is made from eggs, sugar, lemon juice, lemon zest, and butter.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:13.050
But you hardly had any butter left!

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:14.970
I used this as a substitute.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:16.850
Olive oil.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.730
And it's not just any olive oil.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:22.650
That's a very Italian creativity.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:26.070
Indeed, the refreshing fragrance of olives pairs well with the lemons!

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.900
I fell behind with regard 
to the semifreddo's sponge.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:33.950
My sponge would not measure up to biscuit joconde's impact.

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:36.580
I felt I should hedge my bets on the lemon flavor to win this match.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:41.830
I thought that if I could strengthen the lemon's fresh flavor and mellow depth of flavor by using lemon curd,

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:45.790
my semifreddo would not 
pale in comparison to his!

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:49.550
You had an idea to improvise using something from England!

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:53.390
And yet you have succeeded in retaining the dish's Italian roots—your own colors!

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.010
In other words,

00:15:55.510 --> 00:16:00.020
this is a new condiment that should be called Lemon Curd Italiano!

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:05.900
He created a new taste under 
such adverse circumstances.

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.860
<i>Takumi. Isami.</i>

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:13.110
<i>Take this with you when you leave for Japan.</i>

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.530
<i>It's our family's homemade olive oil.</i>

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:19.240
<i>It'll protect you. I'm sure of it.</i>

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.710
The Aldini name protected him.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.960
<i>When I had the flash of inspiration,
 I think I heard a sound.</i>

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:29.340
<i>The sound of changing tracks!</i>

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.630
<i>The sound of my previous recipes being surpassed!</i>

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.510
Oizumi-dono.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:39.770
You seem to have noticed, as well.

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:40.770
Director!

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:48.860
Hey, what's wrong?

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:57.950
What's so funny?

00:16:58.330 --> 00:16:59.790
"What's so funny"?

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:02.040
You say that like I don't know you.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:05.290
I know everything about you!

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:06.210
Right?

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:08.590
You can tell when you compare the two, can't you?

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:11.130
You can tell how deep my semifreddo's flavor is!

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:13.880
I added a secret ingredient, after all!

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:15.840
Preserved lemons.

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:17.930
A traditional Moroccan condiment

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.310
made by salting whole lemons for several weeks!

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:28.690
It is an all-powerful condiment that strengthens acidity, saltiness, bitterness, astringency, and mildness.

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:34.190
I added chopped preserved lemons and their brine to the sponge, praline, and sauce.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:38.700
The faint bitterness is enhancing the semifreddo's sweetness.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:41.870
See, I "trusted" you.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:45.710
I believed that you would draw on the
 flexibility you'd developed in the kitchen,

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:47.620
refuse to give up,

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.710
and add one last twist!

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:54.590
And you always have your good luck charm, the olive oil, close at hand!

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.630
All I had to do was to trace
 your thought processes.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:18:02.510
The only possible conclusion was that you'd go for an Italian-style lemon curd!

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:05.310
You're adorable!

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:07.480
Dancing on my palm!

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:11.360
You didn't even know I saw right through you!

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:15.030
<i>It's such a slim margin!</i>

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:18.780
<i>So minor that you wouldn't notice the difference
 unless you were comparing them directly.</i>

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:20.490
And yet...

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.830
You are driven by two things:

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.790
your bond with your brother, Isami,

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:30.710
and your rematch with Yukihira Souma.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:36.210
How does it feel to have both taken from you at the same time?

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.010
Diablo...

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.720
The judges are in unilateral agreement!

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:43.510
This is my memorable 100th win.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:44.560
I'll be taking this.

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:49.310
The victor in the fourth match
 is Candidate Mimasaka Subaru!

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:53.400
With the conclusion of this match,

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:57.530
the first round of the Autumn Selection is complete!

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:59.150
The second round will occur
 a week from now.

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:03.580
Just like the first round, cards will be drawn to determine the pairings in the second round,

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:05.160
and you'll have the results
 by the end of the day.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:06.500
That is all!

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:37.190
An intensely burning desire was born

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:43.030
But not in me, in someone else

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:47.830
Where's the me who believed that

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:52.960
All one needs is to have hopes and dreams

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:58.210
Wrapped around something long, my compass was lost

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:03.970
On the border of life and death, snow drops bloom

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:09.310
If by some mistake they get smashed

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:14.480
At least put flowers on the empty husk

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:20.150
Is that the way things are? Yes, it is

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:25.200
You can call it resignation if you want

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:31.120
But that's not me, that's not me

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:35.750
There's no value in something just anyone could make

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:40.710
I'm so annoyed!

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:42.420
What's with that stalker?!

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:44.090
I get how you feel,
 so don't take it out on me.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:46.800
Takumi-kun must be in shock...

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:50.600
I want to cheer him up,
 but I don't even know what to say.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:52.310
Oh... Souma-kun?

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:53.640
I'm going back.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:54.310
Huh?

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:57.860
Hey, Yukihira!

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:00.900
Are you sure you didn't need to talk to Takumi?

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:05.070
Hey.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:06.110
Mimasaka?!

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:07.820
Why are you in Yukihira's room?!

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:08.870
A spare key.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:11.540
What do you want?

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:15.000
Oh, I just had something I wanted to report.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.170
Okay, hang on.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:18.500
I'll make some tea.

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:22.670
Oh, Mimasaka, have you eaten dinner?

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:27.140
I have some leftover beef stew. Want some?

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:29.390
Sure, thanks.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:32.600
He should just throw a guy like that out!

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:35.140
Yukihira's hosting him like 
he's just any other guy.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:38.100
The pairings for the second round...

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:40.110
were just announced.

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:41.820
Oh?

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:44.690
It's Kurokiba against Hayama,

00:21:44.690 --> 00:21:48.780
and you against me, Yukihira.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:49.990
Huh.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:52.080
You came all the way here just to tell me that?

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:54.160
You know where I'm
 going with this, right?

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.710
Let's do a Cooking Battle!

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:58.290
The kitchen knife you're always using...

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:01.710
If I win, I'll take that.

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:04.170
In return, if you win, I'll give you this.

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:10.100
<i>Yukihira Souma, I know what really
 gets a rise out of you.</i>

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:15.770
<i>You would never forgive an unjust humiliation of anyone you've come to respect.</i>

00:22:16.690 --> 00:22:19.770
That poor Italian... how pathetic.

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:23.280
He suffered such a major defeat
 before he could face you!

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:26.860
His pride and future as a chef are in tatters!

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:30.660
<i>Well?</i>

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:33.660
<i>Come on, get angry!</i>

00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:37.080
<i>Your precious friend is being ridiculed.</i>

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:40.830
Well... sure, it's disappointing.

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:43.880
But Takumi isn't the kind of guy who'd be ruined by something like this.

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:45.840
One more thing.

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:49.550
You're the one who's pathetic, Mimasaka.

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:51.050
What did you say?

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:53.260
I have a pretty high opinion
 of your skills, you know?

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:58.730
Recreating a dish by someone like Takumi
 would require quite a lot of skill.

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:02.270
But why are you bothering 
with a pointless match like that?

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:08.150
Aldini suffered crushing 
defeat in a "pointless" match.

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:10.570
As a chef, I completely surpass—

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:11.320
You do not.

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:15.040
You just took advantage of Takumi's efforts.

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:21.500
A dish can shine because of the process of going through multiple trials and errors.

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:24.290
You're pathetic.

00:23:24.790 --> 00:23:28.760
You don't know the true joy of cooking.

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:31.220
That's why you can laugh
 about a match like that.

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:35.010
You're robbing people's pride 
through a superficial victory.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:37.180
I can't respect you as a chef for that.

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:39.520
I'll accept your challenge to a Cooking Battle.

00:23:39.520 --> 00:23:42.810
But what I want isn't just the mezzaluna.

00:23:42.810 --> 00:23:47.030
I want the 99 other tools
 you've taken up until now as well.

00:23:47.030 --> 00:23:48.190
Huh?

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:49.780
Don't be ridiculous.

00:23:49.780 --> 00:23:52.240
That doesn't balance out!

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:54.570
What can you give me that's worth a hundred tools?

00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:56.620
Fine, I'll quit being a chef if I lose.

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:03.080
I'll quit being a chef.

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:10.090
Next episode: "The Secret in the First Bite."
